<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Topic//EN" "topic.dtd">
<topic id="git-addon-ignore-by-extension">
    <title>Ignore files by extension</title>
    <body>
    
      <p>To exclude all files with a specific extension (for example, <codeph>.temp</codeph>) from
        Git version control, follow these steps:</p>
    
    <ol>
      <li> On <uicontrol
          conref="uicontrol_terminology.dita#uicontrol_terminology/gs0-git-staging-view"/>
        <uicontrol>></uicontrol>
        <uicontrol conref="uicontrol_terminology.dita#uicontrol_terminology/gs1-unstaged-files"/>,
        select a file with the extension you want to ignore (for example,
        <codeph>file.temp</codeph>). </li>
      <li>
        Right-click the file to open the contextual menu.
      </li>
      <li> From the contextual menu, select <uicontrol
          conref="uicontrol_terminology.dita#uicontrol_terminology/ignore"/> > <uicontrol
          conref="uicontrol_terminology.dita#uicontrol_terminology/ignore-by-extension"/>. <p>
          <fig id="fig_qtj_myd_mjc">
            <title>Ignoring a <codeph>.temp</codeph> file by extension</title>
            <image href="../img/git-addon/staging/ignore/ignore-by-extension.png"
              id="image_g2n_4zd_mjc"/>
          </fig>
        </p></li>
    </ol>
    <p>The extension is added to the project's <codeph>.gitignore</codeph>.</p>
  </body>
</topic>
